  "body": "<!--\nThank you for contributing to the HTML Standard! Please describe the change you are making and complete the checklist below if your change is not editorial.\n-->\n\nPreviously, the table's `height` attribute would not allow dimension values that evaluated to zero after being parsed. Now, the `height` attribute will respect zero.\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\nHopefully not applicable? We're just aligning the spec with current behavior.\n- [ ] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n  https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/40350\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\nN/A, we're aligning the spec with current browser behavior.\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed:\nI don't think we need to do this, I didn't find anything relevant on [the table's MDN page.](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/table)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9374/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jun 2, 2023, 2:10 PM UTC (c03090b)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9374/41a2b50...c03090b/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jun 2, 2023, 2:10 PM UTC (c03090b)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9374/rendering.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jun 2, 2023, 2:10 PM UTC (c03090b)\">/